<title>BELGIUM: City Hotels sees higher 1996 net, dividend.</title>
<headline>City Hotels sees higher 1996 net, dividend.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Estimated results for financial year ending Dec 31, 1996 (in millions of Belgian francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group net profit		 845.0  vs    20.8</p>
<p>    Dividend (francs)		  191  vs	42</p>
<p>    Cons turnover/sales	  1,685.0  vs 6,174.0</p>
<p>    Cons current profit	     45.0  vs    38.3</p>
<p>NOTE - City Hotels operates a number of hotels in North America and Europe. In 1996 it sold off most of its interests in airline  EuroBelgian Airline to the Virgin Group.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
